Title: Nightwatch
Contact: Studio Weber

INT. GRAUFELD LIGHTHOUSE – WATCH ROOM – NIGHT #14#

Night. Fog presses against the panes. A woman sits at the table, a stack of pages in front of her. The door to the gallery opens. The keeper steps in, fog on his shoulders.

KEEPER
Nobody is allowed up here at night.

ILVA BRANDES
(without looking up)
I know. This page was already here. In my handwriting. I never wrote it.

KEEPER
What does it say?

ILVA BRANDES
(reading)
When the light goes out at 3:13, count to seven.

KEEPER
The fire never goes out.

Above them the beam sweeps through the room. Then it goes out. Nobody moves.

ILVA BRANDES
(whispering)
One. Two. Three. Four.

The light returns. The chair is empty. The page is still on the table.
